From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 4 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: Lua library seat checks, disable-field mask, counter
 side and Field Zone lookup at n > 2

The stock code in libduel.cpp and playerop.cpp has sites that only work with
two duelists. With more than 2 duelists they call opponent_of, index an array
with a player value that is not a seat, or ignore seats 2 and 3. Every change is
in an n_duelists > 2 branch (or a test that gives the stock result at n == 2).
The n == 2 behaviour is unchanged.

Duel.SelectDisableField: the opponent half of the zone mask is the next living
duelist in turn order (the duelist that the field-disabled code binds). It is
skipped when no other duelist lives. This was the only opponent_of trap left in
these files.
Duel.GetEnvironment: looks at the Field Zone of every living duelist, not only
seats 0 and 1.
Duel.IncreaseSummonedCount, Duel.CheckSummonedCount: a reason player that is not
a seat does nothing (Increase) or gives false (Check). No read or write of
summon_count out of range.
Duel.GetCustomActivityCount: a player that is not a seat gives 0.
Duel.GetDecktopGroup, GetDeckbottomGroup, GetExtraTopGroup: a player that is not
a seat gives an empty group. Before, a Lua value like 1-tp read out of range.
Duel.CheckReleaseGroup, SelectReleaseGroup (and the Ex forms): the player test
accepts every seat, not only 0 and 1.
Duel.DiscardDeck, Duel.CheckTribute (toplayer), Card.CheckUniqueOnField: a player
that is not a seat gives the empty result (0, false, true = no conflict).
Effect.SetAbsoluteRange: with more than 2 duelists the ranges stay relative to the
owner (s = own side, o = the other side). The swap for a player other than 0 is
only the two-player way to name seat 1. effect::is_target_player reads them so.
playerop SelectCounter: a Tag partner counts as the own side, not the other
side. A player that is not a living seat gets no prompt and no cards.
playerop SelectPlace: the answer must name a living duelist.

Left alone: the other sites in these files were already fixed or are reached
only at n == 2. libgroup.cpp and libeffect.cpp have no opponent_of. The Lua
values 2 and 3 (PLAYER_NONE, PLAYER_ALL) are not changed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
